# Branch strategy

GitHub Flow. No Git Flow `develop`/`release`. Full convention: `AGENTS.md` (Branching).

## Branches

- `main` — shippable. Never commit directly. PR only.
- `integrate/<epic>` — short-lived assembly line. **Current epic base: `integrate/ui-v1`.**
- `feat/<area>-<slug>`, `fix/<slug>`, `chore/<slug>` — one concern, one PR, delete after merge.

Do not keep `cursor/…` names. Open PRs as `feat/…`. Ignore `cursor/backend-frontend-split-6388` (duplicate A0).

## Cut from the right base

1. If `origin/integrate/<epic>` exists, branch from it (Cloud Agents: `cloud_base_branch` = that name).
2. Else branch from up-to-date `origin/main`.
3. Never fork features from stale `main`. That duplicates `frontend/package.json` and Vite apps.

```bash
git fetch origin
git checkout integrate/ui-v1
git pull
git checkout -b feat/ui-queue-packet
```

## Agent / PR rules

- One feature → one branch → one PR into `integrate/ui-v1` (ui-v1 epic) or `main` (no epic).
- Rebase onto the integration branch before merge. Do not merge `main` into the feature as a habit.
- Touch only owned paths. Do not recreate `frontend/package.json`, `vite.config.ts`, or `backend/pyproject.toml` if they already exist on the base.
- Shared magnets (`App.tsx`, `routes.ts`, `docs/FEATURES.md`): sequential PRs, or append-only FEATURES rows.
- No force-push to `main` or `integrate/*`. No secrets in git.

